{#
  The homepage audit tool — the `tools` structure at /tools/{slug}.

  NAMED FOR THE ENTRY TYPE, not `default`. The structure router tries the type before
  falling back (see _routers/structure.twig), and there will be more than one tool here:
  each gets its own type and its own view, which is what lets the next one include a
  different form without this file growing a conditional for every tool ever added.

  Directory is the section HANDLE — the structure router keys off `entry.section.handle`,
  unlike the single router which uses the name. Section handle is `tools`.

  Built on the same `_components/content` shape as the contact single and the generic page,
  so a tool sits in the family rather than looking like a new kind of page.

  THE FORM IS A CASE CONTENT BLOCK, not a slot. It used to be passed as `form` and landed
  beside the columns wherever the component put it; as a `contentHomepageAnalysis` block it
  goes where the argument for it ends, which is an editorial decision and belongs in the CMS.
  No block, no form — a tool page with nothing to fill in is a page that is not finished, and
  that should be visible rather than papered over by a fallback.
#}
{% extends '_layouts/page.twig' %}
{% import '_macros/text' as text %}

{% set tplPath = _self %}

{# Cream slab, as the contact single and the generic page use. #}
{% set slabModifier = 'b-slab--l600' %}

{% block siteContent %}
    {# THE CTAs TRAVEL WITH THE FORM, not with the page. They used to be passed here and
       the component drew them beside the `form` slot; now the form is a Case Content block
       and takes its ways-in box with it, so passing them here as well drew the white panel
       twice — once empty beside nothing, once properly beside the form. See
       _components/case-content, contentHomepageAnalysis. #}

    {# The Summary as a standfirst above the form, exactly as on a generic page: a
       plain-text field, so it is escaped here; blank lines become paragraphs and single
       line breaks stay as breaks. #}
    {% set summary = (entry.summary ?? '')|trim %}
    {% set standfirst = null %}
    {% if summary %}
        {% set standfirst %}
            {% for para in summary|split("\n\n") %}
                <p class="c-content__summary">{{ text.standfirst(para) }}</p>
            {% endfor %}
        {% endset %}
    {% endif %}

    {# Whisper is the entry's TITLE and the h1 is its longTitle: "Homepage Analysis" over
       "The space on your homepage is a budget nobody has ever audited". The short name says
       what the page is, the long one makes the argument, and a reader gets them in that
       order.

       FALLS BACK TO THE SECTION when there is no longTitle, because the h1 falls back to
       the title — and the same words twice, once small and once large, reads as a stutter.
       That was why this was the section's name to begin with. #}
    {# The Case Content builder, rendered to HTML first and handed over finished — the same
       shape the About single and the case studies use. `_components/content` takes markup
       and knows nothing about block types, which is what lets a tool page carry the same
       blocks as a case study without either template learning about the other. #}
    {% set caseBlocks = entry.caseContent.all() %}
    {% set blocks = include('_components/case-content', {
        blocks: caseBlocks,
    }, with_context = false) %}

    {% set heading = entry.longTitle ?: entry.title %}

    {# `blocksAfterBody` puts the blocks BELOW the standfirst, as the About single and the
       notes channel pass it. Without it the component renders blocks above the body and the
       page's own summary ends up under everything it was meant to introduce.

       The comment is out here because a Twig comment INSIDE a hash literal is a syntax error
       and takes the page down with it. #}
    {% include '_components/content' with {
        whisper: heading == entry.title ? entry.section.name : entry.title,
        title: heading,
        body: standfirst,
        blocks: blocks|trim ? blocks : null,
        blocksAfterBody: true,
    } only %}
{% endblock %}
